#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Lifecycle control for the wallpaper runtime.

  fresco set <path-or-workshop-id>   # switch image/live wallpaper (starts if needed)
  fresco clear                       # tear down to idle (static desktop)
  fresco repose [quiet|loud|off]     # toggle the repose cover
                                           # (explicit variant enters/switches)
  fresco repose-bg <scene|desktop>   # cover scene (path, workshop id,
                                           # or "desktop" to mirror it)
  fresco repose-look <zephyr|pixel>  # composition language
  fresco repose-viz <strings|spectrum> # audio visualizer shape
  fresco repose-variant <quiet|loud> # composition arrangement
  fresco repose-grade [on|off]       # backdrop grade treatment
  fresco repose-night [on|off]       # StandBy night tint
  fresco repose-pixels [on|off]      # pixelated visualizer treatment
  fresco repose-label [on|off]       # scene-name label (bottom right)
  fresco repose-pool <scene-id>...   # ordered scenes cycled by arrow keys
  fresco repose-state                # print the persisted state as JSON
  fresco repose-add <path-or-id>     # add a live source to scenes/
  fresco lock-bg [<image>|theme]     # lock-screen wallpaper (the system
                                           # wallpaper — only visible locked)

Repose selection lives in one record (~/.config/fresco/
repose.json: look, scene, scenePool, viz, variant, grade, night, pixels, label); these
subcommands and the in-cover keys (arrows scene, tab look, b visualizer, x pixels,
v variant, g/n treatments, l label) are both thin writers over it,
applied live to an open cover.
  fresco start | stop | restart
  fresco mute [on|off] | unmute        # toggle or set global wallpaper audio
  fresco status
  fresco build                       # (re)compile the daemon binary
  fresco scene-build                 # (re)compile the GPL scene helper
  fresco scene-samples               # seed the measured scene corpus into Livery
  fresco scene-assets [status]
  fresco scene-assets set <path>     # persist a validated owned assets root
  fresco scene-assets validate <path>
  fresco scene-assets clear
  fresco audit [all|current|<id-or-path>...]
                                      # isolated web render checks + evidence
  fresco property [<id-or-path>] list
  fresco property [<id-or-path>] get <name>
  fresco property [<id-or-path>] set <name> <value>
  fresco property [<id-or-path>] reset [<name>]
  fresco audio-permission            # show the stable app to grant once
  fresco install-agent               # launchd agent: start at login
  fresco uninstall-agent

State lives in ~/.config/fresco/: `state.json` is desired policy,
`status.json` is runtime evidence, and `current` is a compatibility projection.
A running daemon reconciles accepted state on SIGUSR1 and refreshes persisted
project properties on SIGHUP. `stop` uses launchctl when the agent is loaded so
KeepAlive doesn't resurrect it.
"""

